      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Financing a roof replacement in Utah is available through contractor-partnered payment plans, home equity options, and government assistance. Rates typically start around 4.99% to 8.99% APR with terms from 12 to 180 months, and many local contractors offer $0-down or 12-month same-as-cash promotional periods.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "contractor-partnered payment plans, home equity options, and government assistance"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Common Financing Methods"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Contractor-Partnered Loans: Many local Utah roofers partner with third-party lenders to provide quick, paperless pre-qualification via soft credit checks.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "HELOC or Home Equity Loans: Utilizing home equity often secures lower interest rates or longer repayment terms (up to 30 years) through local lenders and specialized home improvement programs.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "USDA Section 504 Loans/Grants: Low-income rural or elderly Utah homeowners may qualify for government-backed repair loans up to $20,000 or grants up to $7,500."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Insurance Claims: If your roof suffered storm or hail damage, homeowner's insurance may cover the replacement minus your deductible."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Typical Plan Structures"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Same-As-Cash: 0% interest if paid in full within 12 months."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fixed Monthly Payment:\nLower fixed APR plans spread across 60 to 120 months."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Unsecured vs. Secured: Most fast contractor loans are unsecured personal loans, while equity lines may place a lien on the property."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8,
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your estimated budget\nor project cost"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you prefer low monthly payments or a 0% interest promotional period"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you narrow down the best type of loan or program to look for."
      }
